{"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/ST"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"k-d trees","anchor":"k-d-trees","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/BoundingBox"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KDTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Point"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Point"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SIMDP","text":"SIMD"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Point"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s11SIMDStorageP6ScalarQa","text":"Scalar"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SF","text":"FloatingPoint"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tree splits the points at the median of one coordinate, then splits each half at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"median of the next coordinate, cycling through the dimensions (Bentley, “Multidimensional","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Binary Search Trees Used for Associative Searching”, 1975). It is stored with no links: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"points are permuted so that every subtree is a contiguous run with its median in the middle.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A search descends toward the query and visits the far side of a split only when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"splitting plane is closer than what it has found (Friedman, Bentley and Finkel, 1977).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let tree = KDTree<SIMD2<Double>>([[2, 3], [5, 4], [9, 6], [4, 7], [8, 1], [7, 2]])","tree.nearestIndex(to: [9, 2])                    \/\/ 4: the point [8, 1]","tree.nearestIndices(to: [9, 2], count: 2)        \/\/ [4, 5]","tree.indices(within: 3, of: [5, 5])              \/\/ [1, 3]","tree.indices(in: BoundingBox(lower: [0, 0], upper: [5, 5]))   \/\/ [0, 1]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Points are SIMD vectors of floating-point scalars, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SIMD2<Double>"},{"type":"text","text":" is a point in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plane and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SIMD3<Float>"},{"type":"text","text":" one in space; distances are Euclidean. As a collection, a k-d tree’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements are its points in the order they were given, and searches answer with their indices."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spatialtrees\/kdtree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A k-d tree: a fixed set of points in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"k"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" dimensions that finds the points nearest a query, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"within a radius or a box of it, without testing every point.","type":"text"}],"topicSecti